+/// resolves the durable SqliteControlledExecutionLedger when receipt persistence is enabled
+/// and the in-memory ledger otherwise; pre-cutover in-memory records are non-authoritative
+/// and never imported; durable rows carry an explicit durable-state origin; permission
+/// consumption is never resurrected across cutover or restart; and rolling the switch back to
+/// in-memory leaves all v1 spend rows and all v2 history intact and inert.
