+// ===========================================================================
+// GMF-P2B: AtomicSpendCrashSafetyTests — AC(e).
+//
+// Crash safety is exactly two-outcome (S4): a crash or persistence failure
+// mid-transaction rolls back the entire pre-effect bundle (zero partial
+// writes, permission unconsumed — GMF-NEG-060/P1-C124); a crash after commit
+// leaves exactly the committed set with the permission permanently consumed;
+// and the recovery seam yields COMPLETE (append-only terminal) or
+// ROLLBACK-OF-PENDING-STATE (P2A quarantine) — never un-consuming,
+// resurrecting, or re-spending permission (D21/P1-C108) and never a second
+// effect attempt (P1-C111). Every scenario is injected and observed via raw
+// SQL on a reopened database.
+// ===========================================================================
+
