+// ===========================================================================
+// GMF-P2B: EnvelopeNonAuthorityProofTests — the P1-C048 non-authority proof
+// (checker + checked property) and the GMF-NEG-059 proof case.
+//
+// P1-C046-C052: FleetPermissionEnvelope is a derived executor projection only;
+// an envelope is valid only as a presentation of the referenced canonical
+// IPermission; envelope bytes never decide; and the envelope can never mint,
+// delegate, refresh, or spend authority.
+//
+// The machine-checkable checker binds STRUCTURALLY to real spend paths (R5):
+// IL member-reference/call-graph analysis of the compiled surface (the P2A
+// EffectPathDisabledTests scanner pattern) enumerates every method that can
+// reach a spend-ledger append, transitively, and the checked property asserts
+// "no envelope-only path reaches the spend ledger without canonical IPermission
+// validation". The mutation control ADDS a real envelope-only wrapper member to
+// the compiled surface (Reflection.Emit, with a genuine call to the append
+// primitive) and the checker must FAIL; removing it returns GREEN. The
+// behavioral proof case shows forged/widened/reissued presentations denying
+// FLEET_DENIED_ENVELOPE_FORGERY with the canonical permission unconsumed and
